<%# THE FOCUS PANEL — the one game the reader is watching, at full size.
    Locals: active / upcoming / completed (Game[]) + contest, plus optional
    picked_slugs.

    EVERY GAME IS RENDERED HERE AND ALL BUT ONE IS HIDDEN, which looks wasteful
    until you ask what the alternatives cost. Fetching the chosen game on click
    needs a route, a frame, and a spinner between the click and the picture; and
    the next broadcast would overwrite that frame with whichever game the server
    thought was interesting. Rendering all of them makes switching instant, and
    makes a score update reach the focused game and the fifteen you might switch
    to by exactly the same path as everything else on this page — the broadcast
    that already replaces this whole panel.

    Sixteen tiles is about 30KB of markup. The strip above already draws all
    sixteen twice (the carousel clones its row to loop seamlessly).

    The inline `display:none` is not belt-and-braces for x-show. Alpine boots
    after first paint, so without it every tile is briefly visible and the page
    opens with a column of sixteen games that then collapses to one. %>
<%
  picked_slugs = Array(local_assigns.fetch(:picked_slugs, []))
  phased = active + upcoming + completed
  default_slug = local_assigns.fetch(:focus_slug, nil) || phased.first&.slug
%>
<% if phased.any? %>
  <% phased.each do |game| %>
    <div x-show="focus === '<%= game.slug %>'"
         data-test="live-focus-game"
         data-focus-slug="<%= game.slug %>"
         style="<%= "display: none" unless game.slug == default_slug %>">
      <%= render "live/game_tile", game: game, picked_slugs: picked_slugs, scorers: true %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
<% else %>
  <div class="card p-8 text-center">
    <p class="text-sm text-muted">No games scheduled for this contest yet.</p>
  </div>
<% end %>
